"""Frost Settings: the FrostOS settings app (GTK 4 + libadwaita).

Each page in the sidebar talks to a real part of the system:
  Wi-Fi             NetworkManager (nmcli)
  Bluetooth         BlueZ (bluetoothctl)
  Sound             PipeWire (pactl)
  Displays          Hyprland (hyprctl), saved to ~/.config/frostde/monitors.lua
  Appearance, Dock,
  Notifications     ~/.config/frostde/settings.json (the FrostDE shell watches it)
  Keyboard          Hyprland, saved to ~/.config/frostde/keyboard.lua
  Date & Time       systemd (timedatectl)
  Battery           power-profiles-daemon (powerprofilesctl), UPower (upower)
  Privacy & Security  ufw firewall
  ...

Run with --page <name> to open a page directly, e.g. frost-settings --page wifi
"""

